# Black-box fidelity fixtures — real/confidential documents (C1/C2 but private,
# or personal/RGPD data). NEVER commit or push these. Used locally only to
# drive fidelity QA; committed regression tests use synthetic tests/fixtures/*.pdf.
/tests/fixtures/private/
# QA corpus: the large multi-MB arxiv sample stays local (5.1 MB binary, no code
# references it — used only for interactive sweeps). Small public-domain fixtures
# in corpus-public/ ARE committed for reproducibility.
/tests/fixtures/corpus-public/arxiv-multicol-japanese.pdf
# Safety net: never commit ad-hoc PDFs dropped in the repo root.
/*.pdf
# Vendored OCR assets (tesseract core wasm + worker + traineddata) — generated by
# scripts/prepare-ocr-assets.mjs (npm run ocr:assets). Kept out of git history;
# CI regenerates them before tests/build. See docs/plans/ocr-csp-fix.plan.md.
/public/tesseract/
